   "text": "I read the structure in regions and assembled the SMILES from them.\n\n- **Macrocycle:** a cyclen (12-membered ring with four nitrogens) in which every nitrogen carries a CH2C(=O)NH2 group. One ring carbon, between two adjacent nitrogens, bears a CH2\u2013C6H4 (p-phenylene) group.\n- **Thiourea link:** the para position of that benzene ring carries NH\u2013C(=S)\u2013NH, which connects through (CH2)4 to the \u03b5-carbon of the central lysine.\n- **Central lysine:** its \u03b1-NH is acylated by a C(=O)CH2CH2 unit followed by a triethylene-glycol-type chain, with three ether oxygens and a terminal NH. That NH is acylated by C(=O)CH2\u2013O, which is attached to the quinoline at C7.\n- **Second lysine:** the central lysine's C(=O) forms an amide with the \u03b1-NH of a second lysine, which has a free CO2H. Its \u03b5-NH is acylated by (4-iodophenyl)acetyl.\n- **Quinoline end:** the quinoline C4 carries C(=O)NH\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O)\u2013N linked to a pyrrolidine whose C2 bears B(OH)2.\n- **Stereochemistry:**\n  - Both lysine \u03b1-carbons are drawn with wedges and work out as S, the L configuration.\n  - The boroproline carbon is drawn with a hashed bond to boron and works out as R. That is the same spatial arrangement as L-proline, because boron ranks below the ring carbon in priority.\n  - The ring carbon of the cyclen is drawn with plain bonds, so it gets no stereo label.\n\nI wrote the SMILES with these pieces joined in that order and checked ring closures and atom counts against the drawing.\n\nSMILES: NC(=O)CN1CCN(CC(N)=O)CCN(CC(N)=O)CC(Cc2ccc(NC(=S)NCCCC[C@H](NC(=O)CCOCCOCCOCCNC(=O)COc3ccc4c(C(=O)NCC(=O)N5CCC[C@H]5B(O)O)ccnc4c3)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(=O)Cc3ccc(I)cc3)C(=O)O)cc2)N(CC(N)=O)CC1"
